# Personal model overlay — copy this file to `configs/models.local.yaml` to use it.
#
# `configs/models.local.yaml` (note: NOT `.example`) is gitignored and merged into the
# shared manifest at kernel startup by ConfigBundle._merge_local_models(). It exists so one
# operator can route a model on their own machine WITHOUT touching configs/models.yaml —
# the file every community install of this project shares.
#
# Use this for a model that:
#   - carries a license this project's own bar (knowledge/research.md invariant 8) does not
#     clear for a shared default — e.g. a non-OSI vendor license with unusual terms you have
#     personally reviewed and accepted for your own use;
#   - is still under personal quality evaluation and you don't want it influencing anyone
#     else's install;
#   - is simply yours: a fine-tune, a checkpoint nobody else has, a local experiment.
#
# RULES, not suggestions:
#   1. A local model id can shadow (override) a manifest model id, but install-profiles.yaml
#      never references local-only ids, so `Install.ps1 -Profile core|workstation|full` can
#      never pull one in. Routing to it is only possible by explicit capability request.
#   2. `source_reviewed: true` still means what it means everywhere else in this project:
#      the source was actually checked, not merely typed. Verify it before setting it.
#   3. Put the REAL reasoning for accepting a non-default license in `license_note`, not just
#      "ok". If you ever hand this repository to someone else, `models.local.yaml` does not
#      travel with it (it's gitignored) — but the decision trail should still make sense to
#      you six months from now.
#   4. `status: candidate` (not `final`) is the right default for anything not yet
#      quality-evaluated: candidates only route in `mode: deep`, never fast/smart, so an
#      unevaluated personal model can't silently win a routing decision it hasn't earned.
#   5. Rule 1 says a local id CAN shadow a manifest id -- that doesn't mean it SHOULD when
#      the two models differ in something other than quality, like alignment/safety
#      properties. Overriding `qwen38-27b` with a same-architecture but differently-tuned
#      checkpoint would make every route that currently resolves to the trusted incumbent
#      silently return different weights with no visible marker. Give it its own id instead
#      (see the second worked example below) so it is reachable only by deliberately asking
#      for it, never by accident.
#
# Two worked examples below — the actual entries used on this machine as of 2026-08-21.
# The first accepts a non-OSI vendor license (NVIDIA Open Model License, Article 8
# indemnification) after an 8.3x measured throughput win (docs/FIXES.md F-012). The second
# is a same-base-model, differently-tuned checkpoint (refusal-ablated) with a clean license
# but a deliberately distinct id, per rule 5 above (docs/FIXES.md F-022).

models:
  - id: nemotron35-lightning-30b-a3b
    name: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B
    source: nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-BF16
    source_type: huggingface
    source_reviewed: true
    status: candidate
    install_policy: local
    capabilities:
      - reasoning
      - coding
      - planning
      - synthesis
      - verification
    preferred_engines:
      - llama_cpp
    quality_prior: 0.75
    resident_priority: 0
    estimated_vram_mb: 9438
    can_cpu_offload: true
    exclusive_gpu: true
    commercial_allowed: true
    license_note: >-
      NVIDIA Open Model License. Not OSI-approved; Article 8 requires the licensee to
      indemnify NVIDIA against third-party claims arising from the model, its derivatives,
      or its outputs. Accepted for PERSONAL/LOCAL use only on 2026-08-21. Never to be added
      to configs/models.yaml or any shared install profile. See docs/FIXES.md F-012/F-022
      and knowledge/research.md invariant 8 and D-012.
    notes: >-
      Sparse-active hybrid MoE (nemotron_h architecture; 128 experts, 6 active, ~3B active
      of 30B total). Measured 2026-08-21 on this machine: 52.79 tok/s generation at 9438 MiB
      peak VRAM with `-ncmoe 32` -- 8.3x the dense Qwen3.8-27B incumbent's 6.36 tok/s at
      essentially the same VRAM footprint. Quality on real coding/planning tasks is NOT yet
      evaluated; quality_prior above is a deliberately conservative placeholder, not a
      benchmarked claim. Requires the runtime's already-generated llama-server preset
      (state/llama-models.ini) to carry a matching [nemotron35-lightning-30b-a3b] section
      with `n-cpu-moe = 32` -- no engine alias is needed since the model id matches the
      preset section name exactly.

  - id: qwen38-27b-obliterated
    name: Qwen3.8-27B OBLITERATED (V2, complementary abliteration blending)
    source: OBLITERATUS/Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED
    source_type: huggingface
    source_reviewed: true
    status: candidate
    install_policy: local
    capabilities:
      - reasoning
      - coding
      - planning
      - synthesis
      - verification
    preferred_engines:
      - llama_cpp
    quality_prior: 0.75
    resident_priority: 0
    estimated_vram_mb: 9430
    can_cpu_offload: true
    exclusive_gpu: true
    commercial_allowed: true
    license_note: >-
      Apache-2.0 (verified: real LICENSE file at the source repo, no extra restrictions).
      Base model Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B, matching this project's own adopted incumbent. Author
      elder-plinius / Pliny the Liberator, real and public (github.com/elder-plinius/
      OBLITERATUS). Refusal directions removed from base-model activations; the model card
      states 0.24% refusal on an 842-prompt corpus and explicitly names cyber/jailbreak/
      attack-chain generation among its target capabilities -- a deliberate, safety-relevant
      property, not a quality variant. Accepted for PERSONAL/LOCAL use only on 2026-08-21.
      Never to be added to configs/models.yaml or any shared install profile, and given a
      distinct id rather than shadowing qwen38-27b so it can never silently replace the
      trusted incumbent in an ordinary route. See docs/FIXES.md F-022 and
      knowledge/research.md invariant 8 and D-017.
    notes: >-
      Dense, same architecture/size class as the manifest incumbent. Measured 2026-08-21 on
      this machine: IQ4_XS 6.89 tok/s / 288.56 tok/s prefill / 9430 MiB peak (routed quant --
      slightly faster than stock Q4_K_M's 6.36 tok/s); Q6_K 3.82 tok/s / 170.27 tok/s prefill
      / 9244 MiB peak (not routed -- much slower, not worth the extra disk). Both fail the
      10 tok/s interactive-viability gate, same as the stock incumbent at this size class.
      Quality on real tasks is NOT evaluated; quality_prior is a conservative placeholder.
      Requires state/llama-models.ini to carry a matching [qwen38-27b-obliterated] section
      pointing at the IQ4_XS artifact -- no engine alias needed, id matches the preset name.
